10. How do you implement global exception handling using @ControllerAdvice and @ExceptionHandler?

   1. @ControllerAdvice provides centralized exception handling across controllers.
   2. @ExceptionHandler identifies which exception a particular handler method should handle.
   3. I create a common error response containing status, message, timestamp and request path.
   4. This avoids duplicate try-catch blocks and maintains consistent API error responses.

   Example:

   @RestControllerAdvice
   public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

       @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
       public ResponseEntity<String> handleNotFound(
               ResourceNotFoundException ex) {

           return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                   .body(ex.getMessage());
       }
   }

