   1. Inversion of Control is a principle where the framework manages object creation and dependencies instead of the application managing everything.
   2. Dependency Injection is a technique used to achieve IoC by providing dependencies to an object.
   3. In Spring Boot, the IoC container creates and manages beans.
   4. Constructor injection is generally preferred because it makes dependencies explicit and supports easier testing.

