16. Check whether this MetricsTracker code is thread-safe. Are there any flaws?

   Code:

   public class MetricsTracker {
       private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, LongAdder> pageViews =
           new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

       public void incrementView(String pageId) {
           pageViews.putIfAbsent(pageId, new LongAdder());
           pageViews.get(pageId).increment();
       }
   }

   1. ConcurrentHashMap makes map operations thread-safe, and LongAdder supports efficient concurrent increments.
   2. The current implementation is generally safe for concurrent increments, assuming pageId is valid and entries are not concurrently removed or replaced.
   3. However, putIfAbsent followed by get performs two map operations. We can simplify it using computeIfAbsent().
   4. LongAdder.sum() is not an atomic snapshot while updates are happening, so it is suitable for metrics rather than strict financial or transactional counts.

   Improved code:

   public void incrementView(String pageId) {
       pageViews.computeIfAbsent(pageId, key -> new LongAdder())
                .increment();
   }

--------------------------------------------------

