18. Why can orderRepository.findAll() cause database performance issues with 10,000 orders?

   Entity:

   @Entity
   public class Order {
       @Id
       Long id;

       @OneToMany(fetch = FetchType.LAZY)
       List<OrderItem> items;
   }

   1. findAll() loads all 10,000 Order entities into memory, which can consume significant heap space.
   2. If the application accesses items for every order, Hibernate may execute one additional query per order, causing the N+1 problem.
   3. This can result in thousands of database queries and increased database load.
   4. I would use pagination, DTO projections, JOIN FETCH, EntityGraph or batch fetching depending on the use case.

   Important: LAZY loading alone does not trigger 10,000 queries. The N+1 issue occurs when the lazy collection is accessed for each order.

