   1. I would use a database transaction with row-level locking or an atomic conditional update.
   2. For example, update the active seat count only when it is less than the configured seat limit.
   3. This ensures two concurrent requests cannot acquire the same last available seat.
   4. I would also use a unique checkout ID and idempotency key to prevent duplicate checkout requests.

