   2. Use database indexes on customerId, applicationId, licenseId and userId.
   3. Cache relatively stable license metadata, but always enforce floating-seat limits using an atomic, strongly consistent operation.
   4. Monitor checkout failures, active seats, expired licenses, API latency and service health.

I. Important design patterns

   1. Strategy Pattern – separate validation logic for Perpetual, Subscription, Floating and Trial licenses.
   2. Factory Pattern – create the appropriate license strategy based on license type.
   3. Repository Pattern – isolate database operations from business logic.
   4. Saga Pattern – manage workflows that span multiple services when distributed transactions are required.

