7. How do transactions work in Spring Boot?

   1. We use @Transactional to manage database transactions.
   2. Spring uses proxy-based AOP to intercept method calls and start or join a transaction.
   3. If the method completes successfully, Spring commits the transaction.
   4. By default, RuntimeException and Error trigger rollback, while checked exceptions do not.

   FOLLOW-UP: Why might @Transactional not work?

