8. Explain different transaction propagation types.

   1. REQUIRED: Uses an existing transaction or creates a new one. This is the default.
   2. REQUIRES_NEW: Suspends the existing transaction and starts a new transaction.
   3. SUPPORTS: Uses an existing transaction if available; otherwise executes without one.
   4. MANDATORY: Requires an existing transaction; otherwise throws an exception.
   5. NOT_SUPPORTED: Suspends an existing transaction and executes without a transaction.
   6. NEVER: Throws an exception if an existing transaction is present.
   7. NESTED: Executes within a nested transaction or savepoint if supported by the transaction manager.

