1. Find the second-highest salary from an Employee list with O(n) time complexity.

   APPROACH: Single Pass – No Sorting

   JAVA 8 CODE:

   public static double secondHighestSalary(List<Employee> employees) {

       double highest = Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;
       double secondHighest = Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;

       for (Employee emp : employees) {
           double salary = emp.getSalary();

           if (salary > highest) {
               secondHighest = highest;
               highest = salary;
           } else if (salary > secondHighest && salary < highest) {
               secondHighest = salary;
           }
       }

       if (secondHighest == Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY) {
           throw new IllegalArgumentException("Second highest salary not found");
       }

       return secondHighest;
   }

   EXPLANATION:
   1. Maintain two variables: highest and secondHighest.
   2. If the current salary is greater than highest, move highest into secondHighest.
   3. Otherwise, if it is between highest and secondHighest, update secondHighest.
   4. Return secondHighest after completing one iteration over the list.

   Time Complexity: O(n)
   Space Complexity: O(1)

